infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Instrumentation cost ladder — reach for the cheapest first
  desc Per-operation CPU overhead climbs: pub/sub → request context → raw hooks
  order asc
  sequences
    - label diagnostics_channel — ~free unless subscribed
      desc In-process pub/sub; a hasSubscribers guard makes an unobserved publish essentially free, so it stays in hot paths. Reach for it first.
    - label AsyncLocalStorage — single-digit % CPU
      desc Request-scoped store that survives await and callbacks; the well-optimized async_hooks consumer. Keep the store small — ids and flags.
    - label raw async_hooks — double-digit % CPU
      desc init/before/after/destroy fires on every timer, socket, and promise. Drop to it only for tracking you can't get otherwise — and measure.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #6366f1 #f43f5e
